---

<DocsLayout
  title="Joomla"
  description="Joomla authentication plugin for DID-based login. Under development (ATT-487). Supports Joomla 4.x and 5.x."
  currentPath="/docs/integration/joomla/"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <h1>Joomla</h1>

  <Callout type="warning">
    <p>
      <strong>This plugin is under development</strong> (ATT-487). The
      information below describes planned functionality. For immediate
      integration, use the
      <a href="/docs/integration/javascript/">JavaScript guide</a> to add
      DID login manually.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Why Joomla Matters</h2>
  <p>
    Many Costa Rican government websites and institutional portals run on
    Joomla. A native authentication plugin ensures these sites can adopt
    DID-based identity without custom development.
  </p>

  <h2>What the Plugin Will Do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Authentication plugin</strong> — integrates with Joomla's authentication framework as a standard plugin</li>
    <li><strong>Admin configuration</strong> — trusted issuers, resolver URL, and login behavior configurable from the Joomla admin panel</li>
    <li><strong>Joomla 4.x and 5.x</strong> — compatible with current Joomla LTS releases</li>
    <li><strong>User group mapping</strong> — map credential types to Joomla user groups (e.g., professional license holders get elevated access)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Planned Configuration</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="XML" title="attestto-auth.xml">
    <Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">&lt;extension</span> <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"plugin"</span> <span class="c-attr">group</span>=<span class="c-str">"authentication"</span><span class="c-kw">&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-kw">&lt;name&gt;</span>plg_authentication_attestto<span class="c-kw">&lt;/name&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-kw">&lt;version&gt;</span>1.0.0<span class="c-kw">&lt;/version&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-kw">&lt;description&gt;</span>DID-based authentication for Joomla<span class="c-kw">&lt;/description&gt;</span>

  <span class="c-kw">&lt;config&gt;</span>
    <span class="c-kw">&lt;fields&gt;</span>
      <span class="c-kw">&lt;fieldset</span> <span class="c-attr">name</span>=<span class="c-str">"basic"</span><span class="c-kw">&gt;</span>
        <span class="c-kw">&lt;field</span> <span class="c-attr">name</span>=<span class="c-str">"resolver_url"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"url"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">default</span>=<span class="c-str">"https://resolver.attestto.com"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">label</span>=<span class="c-str">"DID Resolver URL"</span> <span class="c-kw">/&gt;</span>
        <span class="c-kw">&lt;field</span> <span class="c-attr">name</span>=<span class="c-str">"trusted_issuers"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"textarea"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">label</span>=<span class="c-str">"Trusted Issuers (one DID per line)"</span> <span class="c-kw">/&gt;</span>
        <span class="c-kw">&lt;field</span> <span class="c-attr">name</span>=<span class="c-str">"auto_register"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"radio"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">default</span>=<span class="c-str">"1"</span>
          <span class="c-attr">label</span>=<span class="c-str">"Auto-register new users"</span> <span class="c-kw">/&gt;</span>
      <span class="c-kw">&lt;/fieldset&gt;</span>
    <span class="c-kw">&lt;/fields&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-kw">&lt;/config&gt;</span>
<span class="c-kw">&lt;/extension&gt;</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Planned Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Login module override</strong> — replace the default login form with a DID login button</li>
    <li><strong>Credential-gated content</strong> — restrict articles or menu items to users with specific credential types</li>
    <li><strong>Audit log</strong> — track DID-based authentication events in the Joomla log</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Manual Approach (Available Now)</h2>
  <p>
    Until the plugin ships, use the
    <a href="/docs/integration/javascript/">vanilla JavaScript approach</a>.
    Add the adapter script to your Joomla template's <code>index.php</code>
    or use a custom HTML module:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="HTML">
    <Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">&lt;script</span>
  <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"module"</span>
  <span class="c-attr">src</span>=<span class="c-str">"https://cdn.attestto.com/id-wallet-adapter/0.4.1/index.mjs"</span>
<span class="c-kw">&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</span>

<span class="c-kw">&lt;button</span> <span class="c-attr">id</span>=<span class="c-str">"did-login"</span><span class="c-kw">&gt;</span>Sign in with DID<span class="c-kw">&lt;/button&gt;</span>

<span class="c-kw">&lt;script</span> <span class="c-attr">type</span>=<span class="c-str">"module"</span><span class="c-kw">&gt;</span>
  <span class="c-kw">import</span> { pickWallet } <span class="c-kw">from</span>
    <span class="c-str">'https://cdn.attestto.com/id-wallet-adapter/0.4.1/index.mjs'</span>

  document.<span class="c-fn">getElementById</span><span class="c-br">(</span><span class="c-str">'did-login'</span><span class="c-br">)</span>
    .<span class="c-fn">addEventListener</span><span class="c-br">(</span><span class="c-str">'click'</span>, <span class="c-kw">async</span> <span class="c-br">(</span><span class="c-br">)</span> <span class="c-kw">=&gt;</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
      <span class="c-kw">const</span> wallet = <span class="c-kw">await</span> <span class="c-fn">pickWallet</span><span class="c-br">(</span><span class="c-br">{</span> <span class="c-attr">render</span>: <span class="c-str">'modal'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span><span class="c-br">)</span>
      <span class="c-cm">// Continue with VP request and backend verify</span>
      <span class="c-cm">// See JavaScript guide for full example</span>
    <span class="c-br">}</span><span class="c-br">)</span>
<span class="c-kw">&lt;/script&gt;</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>
</DocsLayout>
